cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use these AI workflows in your research or projects,
  please cite the repository as below.
title: "IWAC AI Pipelines"
version: 1.3.0
date-released: 2026-10-06
abstract: >-
  Python pipelines that apply large language models to the curation of a
  digital archive: OCR extraction and correction, handwritten text
  recognition, bilingual summarization, named-entity recognition and subject
  indexing with authority reconciliation, audio, video and YouTube
  transcription, magazine and scholarly-publication extraction, and sentiment
  analysis, all written back to an Omeka S instance with model provenance
  recorded in the archive. Built for the Islam West Africa Collection (IWAC) and
  adaptable to other digital humanities and social science collections.
type: software
keywords:
  - digital humanities
  - Islam West Africa
  - large language models
  - Omeka S
  - optical character recognition
  - named entity recognition
  - handwritten text recognition
  - digital archives
  - African studies
